Keep the masked-tile skip of tiled flash attention on the measured vendor.

The skip reads the mask before a tile is staged or scored, with a
subgroupMax over the lanes and a shared row_live array. It was measured
on NVIDIA only, and a wrong live decision is a wrong attention sum: a
tile wrongly skipped drops real cells, a row wrongly skipped leaves stale
sums. GCN/Vega wave64 devices run this tile shader for every decode step
when the vec kernel is off, and their subgroup ops are the ones that
have miscompiled before.

The shader takes the skip only with a SKIP_MASKED_TILES define now, and
the pipeline adds that define for an nvidia adapter only. Every other
vendor compiles the tile shader as it was before the skip: each tile is
staged and scored, and a row is bounded only by its own row_active,
the decode of the shipped 1.3.0 build. NVIDIA keeps the skip and pays
one string compare; the variant name records the difference.

diff --git a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/flash_attn_tile.wgsl b/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/flash_attn_tile.wgsl
--- a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/flash_attn_tile.wgsl
+++ b/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/wgsl-shaders/flash_attn_tile.wgsl
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 
 var<workgroup> q_shmem: array<Q_TYPE, Q_TILE * HEAD_DIM_QK>;
 var<workgroup> p_shmem: array<f16, Q_TILE * KV_TILE>;
-#ifdef MASK
+#if defined(MASK) && defined(SKIP_MASKED_TILES)
 // Per query row of the workgroup: 1 when the row may attend to a cell of the KV tile in hand.
 var<workgroup> row_live: array<u32, Q_TILE>;
 #endif
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@
             local_scores[slot] = FLOAT_MIN;
         }
 
-#ifdef MASK
+#if defined(MASK) && defined(SKIP_MASKED_TILES)
         // A cell masked with -inf scores -inf whatever K holds: it cannot raise the running
         // maximum, and its weight is exp(-inf) = 0. A tile that every row of the workgroup has
         // masked out leaves the sums as they are, so its K and V are not staged. With several

